# Formatting for this project's own sources: common/, filter/, static/.
#
# Approximates the nginx coding style, so these modules read like the server
# they are built into: four-space indent, 80 columns, "type *name" pointers,
# the return type of a definition on its own line with the brace under it, and
# braces on the same line for everything else.
#
# clang-format cannot reach nginx style exactly. Two known gaps:
#
#   * nginx aligns the names in a declaration block into a column, with the
#     width chosen per function. AlignConsecutiveDeclarations aligns them, but
#     to clang-format's own width rather than nginx's, so blocks look close
#     rather than identical.
#
#   * nginx separates top-level definitions by two blank lines.
#     MaxEmptyLinesToKeep preserves two where they are written but will not
#     insert them, so that spacing is maintained by hand.
#
# InsertBraces requires clang-format 15 or newer. On an older version the
# option is ignored with a warning and the rest of the style still applies.
#
# Caveat: clang-format searches upwards from the file it is formatting, so
# this file also covers deps/brotli. That is a vendored submodule with its
# own conventions - do not reformat anything under deps/.
---
BasedOnStyle: LLVM
AlignAfterOpenBracket: DontAlign
AlignConsecutiveDeclarations: true
AllowAllArgumentsOnNextLine: false
AllowAllParametersOfDeclarationOnNextLine: false
AllowShortFunctionsOnASingleLine: None
AllowShortIfStatementsOnASingleLine: false
AllowShortLoopsOnASingleLine: false
BreakAfterReturnType: AllDefinitions
BreakBeforeBraces: Linux
ColumnLimit: 80
ContinuationIndentWidth: 4
DerivePointerAlignment: false
IndentCaseLabels: true
IndentWidth: 4
InsertBraces: true
KeepEmptyLinesAtTheStartOfBlocks: false
MaxEmptyLinesToKeep: 2
PointerAlignment: Right
SortIncludes: Never
SpaceAfterCStyleCast: true
